dcomp for Edge WebView2 (Adobe Creative Cloud installer / app sign-in pages).

This is wine-staging v11.10's dcomp-DCompositionCreateDevice2 patchset
(patches 0001-0066, dlls/dcomp only, tests dropped), applied on Wine 11.10.
The shared-visual handle code (staging-only wineserver requests) is stubbed
out so the DLL works with any wineserver version; WebView2 does not use it.

Why the pre-June version: wine-staging 11.11+ adds patch 0067
"dcomp: Allow IDCompositionDevice3 interface". With it, Chromium (WebView2
149+) accepts wine's device and takes its DirectComposition path, then
aborts (int3) when the stubbed IDCompositionVisual::SetClipObject returns
E_NOTIMPL. The gpu-process restarts every ~4 s, each restart maps another
private ~300 MB copy of msedge.dll, and RAM runs away. Without 0067 the
Device3 query fails, Chromium falls back to its HWND swapchain path, and the
page renders (via DXVK's dummy composition swapchain).

Source: https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine-staging/-/tree/v11.10/patches/dcomp-DCompositionCreateDevice2
